===Noun===
{{en-noun|penknives}}

# A small [[pocketknife]]; ''([[Appendix:Glossary#loosely|loosely]])'' any pocketknife.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1948|author=G. Rabel|title=Discovery|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=vAo-AAAAIAAJ&pg=PA17|passage=The [[logical]] [[distinction]] between [[genus]] and [[species]] can, of course, [[apply]] to any [[object]]s [[whatsoever]]. Thus, for [[example]], the genus knife may be divided into several species, such as '''penknife''', table knife, bread knife, [[razor]], etc. We might define the '''penknife''' as a knife small enough to be carried in the pocket, with foldable, sheathable [[elements]], [[characterize]]d by the [[feature]] that one [[blade]] at least is always suitable for sharpening pencils and [[erasing]] ink spots. We are quite sure in which features all the members of a certain species agree, [[notwithstanding]] possible individual characteristics, say a [[monogram]] on one '''penknife''', or a [[corkscrew]] in another.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A small knife designed for safe and convenient storage, typically in the form of a miniature [[clasp-knife]], or with blade [[retractable]] into the handle.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1906|author=Rudyard Kipling|title=Puck of Pook's Hill|passage=Presently the man took a [[reed pen]] from his satchel, and trimmed it with a little ivory knife, carved in the semblance of a fish.<br>"Oh, what a beauty!" cried Dan.<br> "’Ware fingers! That blade is perilous sharp. I made it myself of the best Low Country crossbow steel. And so, too, this fish. When his back-fin travels to his tail — so — he swallows up the blade, even as the whale swallowed Gaffer Jonah."}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A small knife for cutting the points of [[quill]] feathers or [[reed]]s into [[nib]]s to provide or repair writing implements, early versions were commonly small [[sheath knife|sheath knives]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1689|author=John Flavel|title=Christ Knocking at the Door|passage= Every sin is [[damning]] without Christ. "The wages of sin is death". It is no great difference, if a man be killed, whether it be by a [[sword]] or a '''penknife'''. The least sin [[violate]]s the whole law. He that [[offend]]eth in one point, is guilty of all. |url=https://archive.org/details/christknockinga00socigoog}}

